{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Python code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Python 3 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Python 3 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n<your_rewritten_code_2>\ndef solve(n, mod):\n    if n <= 3:\n        return 0\n    \n    last_ans = 17\n    ans = 17\n    size = (n - 1) * (n - 2) // 2 + 1\n    \n    # Initialize DP table with explicit dimensions\n    record = [[0 for _ in range(size + 1)] for _ in range(2)]\n    for i in range(4):\n        record[0][i] = [1, 2, 2, 1][i]\n    \n    inv = 0\n    \n    for m in range(4, n):\n        tp_size = m * (m - 1) // 2\n        ans = (m + 1) * last_ans\n        \n        # First segment: cumulative sums\n        cumsum = 0\n        for i in range(m):\n            cumsum += record[inv ^ 1][i]\n            record[inv][i] = cumsum % mod\n        \n        # Second segment: sliding window sums\n        for i in range(m, tp_size // 2 + 1):\n            cumsum += record[inv ^ 1][i]\n            cumsum -= record[inv ^ 1][i - m]\n            record[inv][i] = cumsum % mod\n        \n        # Third segment: reflection\n        for i in range(tp_size // 2 + 1):\n            record[inv][tp_size - i] = record[inv][i]\n        \n        # Fourth segment: contribution calculation\n        running_total = 0\n        for i in range(tp_size - 1):\n            contrib = 0\n            lo = max(1, -tp_size + i + m + 2)\n            for j in range(lo, m + 1):\n                contrib += j * int(record[inv][m + 2 - j + i])\n            \n            running_total += int(record[inv][i])\n            running_total %= mod\n            contrib *= running_total\n            contrib %= mod\n            ans += contrib\n            ans %= mod\n        \n        last_ans = ans\n        inv ^= 1\n    \n    return int(ans) % mod\n\n\ndef main():\n    n, mod = map(int, input().split())\n    print(solve(n, mod))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</your_rewritten_code_2>\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong long solve(int n, long long mod) {\n    if (n <= 3) {\n        return 0;\n    }\n    \n    long long last_ans = 17;\n    long long ans = 17;\n    int size = (n - 1) * (n - 2) / 2 + 1;\n    \n    // Initialize DP table with explicit dimensions\n    vector<vector<long long>> record(2, vector<long long>(size + 1, 0));\n    for (int i = 0; i < 4; i++) {\n        record[0][i] = (long long)(vector<int>{1, 2, 2, 1}[i]);\n    }\n    \n    int inv = 0;\n    \n    for (int m = 4; m < n; m++) {\n        int tp_size = m * (m - 1) / 2;\n        ans = (m + 1) * last_ans;\n        \n        // First segment: cumulative sums\n        long long cumsum = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < m; i++) {\n            cumsum += record[inv ^ 1][i];\n            record[inv][i] = cumsum % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Second segment: sliding window sums\n        for (int i = m; i <= tp_size / 2; i++) {\n            cumsum += record[inv ^ 1][i];\n            cumsum -= record[inv ^ 1][i - m];\n            record[inv][i] = cumsum % mod;\n        }\n        \n        // Third segment: reflection\n        for (int i = 0; i <= tp_size / 2; i++) {\n            record[inv][tp_size - i] = record[inv][i];\n        }\n        \n        // Fourth segment: contribution calculation\n        long long running_total = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < tp_size - 1; i++) {\n            long long contrib = 0;\n            int lo = max(1, -tp_size + i + m + 2);\n            for (int j = lo; j <= m; j++) {\n                contrib += j * record[inv][m + 2 - j + i];\n            }\n            \n            running_total += record[inv][i];\n            running_total %= mod;\n            contrib *= running_total;\n            contrib %= mod;\n            ans += contrib;\n            ans %= mod;\n        }\n        \n        last_ans = ans;\n        inv ^= 1;\n    }\n    \n    return (int)(ans % mod);\n}\n\nint main() {\n    int n, mod;\n    cin >> n >> mod;\n    cout << solve(n, mod) << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.35\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.00024291902082040906, -2.264974000354414e-06, -1.4305104514278355e-06, -0.0004711233195848763, -5.960462772236497e-07, -7.045020902296528e-05, -1.7881377516459906e-06, -2.288792165927589e-05, 0.0, -1.1801649634435307e-05, -3.5523738915799186e-05, -0.04859470948576927, -1.9073304429184645e-05, -0.0003375437227077782, -0.6326032876968384, -0.009809738956391811, -1.1801649634435307e-05, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.10149264335632324, -6.556489552167477e-06, -0.00025185750564560294, -0.5231508612632751, -7.152555099310121e-07, -4.172316494077677e-06, -0.474079430103302, -2.0265558760002023e-06, -8.344646857949556e-07, -2.3841830625315197e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -2.0503786799963564e-05, -0.001505790394730866, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -3.576278118089249e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.0001793938863556832, -2.384185